  "methodology": "Same corpus, same ground truth, same source detectors. Only the arbitration rule differs, switched by DIABLO_ARBITRATION. Three runs per arm because the vision model is sampled and not deterministic: a single run of each arm produced 72% vs 60% and two wrong targets, all of which were vision variance rather than arbitration. Figures below are per-run values that were identical across all three runs unless a range is given.",
  "old_algorithm": "ambiguous = margin < AMBIGUOUS_WITHIN (0.12), a flat absolute threshold applied at every confidence level.",
  "new_algorithm": "resolved = separation > SEPARATION * (1 - basis), SEPARATION = 2 * AMBIGUOUS_WITHIN = 0.24, strictly greater. When the top candidate's corroboration does not distinguish it from the runner-up, both the separation and the basis come from each candidate's strongest single source instead of the fused figures.",
